    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48963": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art (Studio Art)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Art (Studio Art) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Art (Studio Art) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit the following: • cover letter • a detailed CV • statement of teaching philosophy • statement of research (artist’s statement) • names and contact information of three references • samples of personal work • samples of student work - for time-based media work examples, please provide URLs for each specific project within a PDF document and submit under “media presentation” in the supplemental documents section of the application. Applicants that have access to their letters of recommendation can upload them in the supplemental documents section, if they would like. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted . Candidates selected for finalist interviews will need to provide written letters of recommendation, and official transcripts for completed degrees. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Art (Studio Art) Requisition 202600135F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Arts & Media Department Dept of Art Open Date 10/16/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48871 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Rebecca Finley Title Chair Department of Art PO Box 2089 Huntsville, Texas 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-1314 Contact Email rlf001@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Art at Sam Houston State University invites applicants for a full-time Assistant Professor of Art, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The successful candidate will have an emphasis in Drawing and a studio practice that demonstrates versatility across a range of practices, with the capacity to contribute to foundational through graduate instruction. These areas could include ceramics, digital art, foundations, illustration, interdisciplinary, performance and video, painting, photography, printmaking, or sculpture. Artists engaged in hybrid art forms and / or community engagement are preferred, as well as those whose work reflects innovative approaches that extend the boundaries of traditional media. Primary responsibilities include teaching a 3/2 course load, contributing to departmental service through committee participation, and research in area of emphasis. Ongoing creative accomplishments, exhibitions, and research are an expectation. Learn more about the SHSU Department of Art at www.shsu.edu/art Educational Requirements for the Position Applicants must have an MFA in Art. Experience Required for the Position Experience teaching at the undergraduate level. Graduate teaching experience is preferred. Other Requirements for the Position The successful candidate will have an ongoing, sustainable, and engaged art practice, and be prepared to be an active faculty member who is engaged with the department, college, University, local and professional communities. Special Instructions Summary Applicants should submit the following: • cover letter • a detailed CV • statement of teaching philosophy • statement of research (artist’s statement) • names and contact information of three references • samples of personal work • samples of student work – for time-based media work examples, please provide URLs for each specific project within a PDF document and submit under “media presentation” in the supplemental documents section of the application. Applicants that have access to their letters of recommendation can upload them in the supplemental documents section, if they would like. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted . Candidates selected for finalist interviews will need to provide written letters of recommendation, and official transcripts for completed degrees. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Teaching Portfolio Media Presentation Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Transcripts Web Site Sample © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
