    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48913": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Psychology (Up to 4 positions to be Filled)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Psychology (Up to 4 positions to be Filled) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Psychology (Up to 4 positions to be Filled) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Psychology (Up to 4 positions to be Filled) Requisition 202600126F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Dept of Psychology and Philosophy Open Date 10/12/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48717 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Hillary Langley Title Associate Department Chair Sam Houston State University Department of Psychology and Philosophy Box 2447 Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-3260 Contact Email hlangley@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The instructors for these pool faculty positions will be hired to teach a broad range of undergraduate courses in psychology, ranging from introductory psychology to more advanced courses at the 3000- and 4000-level. The department is searching for instructors to teach courses related to the basic science of psychology (e.g., developmental psychology, social psychology, physiological psychology, research methods, statistics) as well as applied areas (abnormal psychology, psychology and law, psychopharmacology). All applicants will be considered, but the department especially needs instructors who can teach in-person courses. Educational Requirements for the Position Requires a minimum of master’s degree in related field for lower level course offerings. Experience Required for the Position Teaching experience preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Special Instructions Summary References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to teach during the day? Yes No * Are you available to teach during the evening? Yes No Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
