    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48872": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice &amp; Criminology (up to 4 positions)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice &amp; Criminology (up to 4 positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice & Criminology (up to 4 positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted online at: https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/ and should include a letter of interest, a current vita, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research & goals, and the names and contact information for three references. addressed to: : Dr. Andia Azimi (axa205@shsu.edu), Chair Search Committee, Department of Criminal Justice and Criminology, Sam Houston State University, Huntsville, Texas 77341-2296. Review of materials will begin September 16, 2026, and will continue until the search is completed. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Criminal Justice & Criminology (up to 4 positions) Requisition 202600109F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Criminal Justice Department Dept of Criminal Justice and Criminology Open Date 08/17/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48267 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Andia Azimi Title Search Committee Chair Department of Criminal Justice and Criminology Sam Houston State University Huntsville, Texas 77341-2296 Contact Phone Contact Email axa205@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Successful applicants are expected to 1) have an active research agenda that includes a strong publication record; 2) demonstrate the potential to secure external research funding; 3) teach core courses in the Department’s academic degree programs; and 4) demonstrate a commitment to mentoring students. Educational Requirements for the Position Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related academic field. Experience Required for the Position Areas of specialization are open, but preference will be given to candidates with research expertise in policing or juvenile justice and delinquency. Other Requirements for the Position The faculty positions will be on-site with in-person teaching expectations and research expectations that are consistent with a high-ranking doctoral degree granting department within an R2 university. Special Instructions Summary To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted online at: https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/ and should include a letter of interest, a current vita, statement of teaching philosophy, statement of research & goals, and the names and contact information for three references. addressed to: : Dr. Andia Azimi (axa205@shsu.edu), Chair Search Committee, Department of Criminal Justice and Criminology, Sam Houston State University, Huntsville, Texas 77341-2296. Review of materials will begin September 16, 2026, and will continue until the search is completed. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Reference Contact Information Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48870": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Political Science (2026-2027) - up to 3 positions to be filled",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Political Science (2026-2027) - up to 3 positions to be filled Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Political Science (2026-2027) - up to 3 positions to be filled Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Political Science (2026-2027) - up to 3 positions to be filled Requisition 202600132F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Salary commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Humanities and Social Sciences Department Dept of Political Science Open Date 10/06/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48764 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Jonathan Brown Title Associate Professor and Chair Department of Political Science Sam Houston State University Box 2149 Huntsville, TX 77341-2149 Contact Phone 936-294-4478 Contact Email jnb047@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Political Science seeks a qualified instructor to teach American Government and/or Texas Government during the Spring 2027 term. Courses could be taught either online or face-to-face at the main Sam Houston State University campus in Huntsville, TX. Educational Requirements for the Position Master’s degree or Ph.D. in political science preferred; will also consider those that meet SACSCOC credentialing requirements of a Master’s degree in a different field plus 18-graduate credits in political science. Experience Required for the Position Teaching experience, especially online-teaching experience, is preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Are you a current Sam Houston State University employee? Yes No * Are you available to teach during the day? Yes No * Are you available to teach during the evening? Yes No Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Transcripts Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
