    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48851": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art (Graphic Design)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Art (Graphic Design) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Art (Graphic Design) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit the following documents as PDF: cover letter a detailed CV statement of teaching philosophy statement describing research and goals names and contact information of three references samples of personal work samples of student work- – for time-based media work examples, please provide URLs for each specific project within the PDF document. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. The Department of Art www.shsu.edu/art has about 700 undergraduate majors in Graphic Design, Studio Art, Photography, and Animation, and offers an MFA in Art and Social Practice. The Dana G. Hoyt Fine Arts Building includes state of the art lecture halls and classrooms, studios, computer labs, and galleries. In addition to the University Art Gallery on campus, the Department exhibits student work at a Satellite Gallery in downtown Huntsville and has MFA studios in the Natural Science and Art Research Center a few blocks away. Sam Houston State University is located 70 miles north of Houston in Huntsville, TX, surrounded by the Sam Houston National Forest. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Art (Graphic Design) Requisition 202600131F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Arts & Media Department Dept of Art Open Date 10/05/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48734 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Rebecca Finley Title Chair Department of Art PO Box 2089 Huntsville, Texas 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-1314 Contact Email rlf001@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Art at Sam Houston State University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Art in Graphic Design, beginning Fall 2027. We are seeking an innovative and dedicated educator whose practice bridges print, interactive, and emerging design fields, with demonstrated expertise in contemporary design technologies and a willingness to explore and integrate AI-driven tools and emerging workflows. The ideal candidate will demonstrate the ability to adapt to evolving industry standards and to prepare students for careers in a rapidly changing creative landscape. A strong commitment to foundational design principles, conceptual development, and research-based , forward-thinking design pedagogy is essential. Duties include teaching 5 courses per year (3/2 course load), service on departmental, college, and university committees, and include an expectation of sustained, peer-reviewed creative activity or scholarly research. Educational Requirements for the Position Candidates must possess an MFA or terminal degree in Graphic Design or Visual Communications and demonstrate outstanding potential in research and/or creative activity. Experience Required for the Position Teaching experience at the undergraduate level is strongly preferred. Professional Design experience is also an asset. Other Requirements for the Position The successful candidate will be expected to teach a range of undergraduate Graphic Design courses, including, but not limited to Principles of Graphic Design, Typography, Corporate Identity Design, UX/UI, Motion Graphics, and Senior Studio in Graphic Design. Applicants should present a professional portfolio demonstrating significant achievement in graphic design and/or related areas of contemporary design practice. Mastery of Adobe Creative Suite is required. Proficiency in web development practices, Figma, and other relevant interactive design tools is expected. Additional responsibilities include: Incorporating AI applications and emerging technologies into coursework Guiding students in production design using equipment such as 3D printers and die cutters Developing and maintaining a forward-thinking curriculum aligned with current industry standards Demonstrating strong communication, collaboration, and interpersonal skills Contributing to the growth and vision of a regionally competitive Graphic Design program Mentoring students in career preparation, internships, and professional development Building connections with design professionals, organizations, and industry partners Special Instructions Summary Applicants should submit the following documents as PDF : cover letter a detailed CV statement of teaching philosophy statement describing research and goals names and contact information of three references samples of personal work samples of student work- – for time-based media work examples, please provide URLs for each specific project within the PDF document. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. The Department of Art www.shsu.edu/art has about 700 undergraduate majors in Graphic Design, Studio Art, Photography, and Animation, and offers an MFA in Art and Social Practice. The Dana G. Hoyt Fine Arts Building includes state of the art lecture halls and classrooms, studios, computer labs, and galleries. In addition to the University Art Gallery on campus, the Department exhibits student work at a Satellite Gallery in downtown Huntsville and has MFA studios in the Natural Science and Art Research Center a few blocks away. Sam Houston State University is located 70 miles north of Houston in Huntsville, TX, surrounded by the Sam Houston National Forest. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Media Presentation Transcripts Reference Contact Information Teaching Portfolio Optional Documents Web Site Sample © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
