    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48748": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Chemistry (3 positions to be filled)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Chemistry (3 positions to be filled) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Chemistry (3 positions to be filled) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of application materials will begin October 23, 2026, and will continue until position is filled. Interested candidates should submit an application letter, curriculum vitae, transcripts, research plan, teaching statement (including courses taught and courses the candidate is qualified to teach), and letters of recommendation at http://shsu.peopleadmin.com. Please note that references provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email requesting a letter of recommendation when the application is submitted. Three letters of recommendation are required. References will submit their letters through the reference link provided in the automated email from PeopleAdmin. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Chemistry (3 positions to be filled) Requisition 202600124F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Salary commensurate with experience and education. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Chemistry Open Date 09/28/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48541 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Dustin E. Gross Title Department of Chemistry Sam Houston State University Box 2117 Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-1532 Contact Email deg013@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Chemistry at Sam Houston State University is growing and seeks to hire three tenure-track faculty members in physical chemistry, inorganic chemistry, and related or multidisciplinary areas of chemistry. Responsibilities include establishing a vigorous, externally fundable research program; mentoring and supervising undergraduate and graduate research students; and delivering excellent, engaging instruction in courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise. The successful candidates will contribute to the department’s ACS -certified B.S. in Chemistry, B.S. in Forensic Chemistry, and M.S. in Chemistry programs through undergraduate and graduate instruction, thesis advising, and graduate student recruitment. Educational Requirements for the Position Ph.D. in Chemistry. Experience Required for the Position We seek physical chemists, inorganic chemists, and multidisciplinary chemists whose expertise complements the department’s existing programs and expands opportunities for research and instruction. Postdoctoral research experience is preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Excellent written and verbal communication skills. The position will begin Fall 2027. Special Instructions Summary Review of application materials will begin October 23, 2026, and will continue until position is filled. Interested candidates should submit an application letter, curriculum vitae, transcripts, research plan, teaching statement (including courses taught and courses the candidate is qualified to teach), and letters of recommendation at http://shsu.peopleadmin.com. Please note that references provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email requesting a letter of recommendation when the application is submitted. Three letters of recommendation are required. References will submit their letters through the reference link provided in the automated email from PeopleAdmin. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to teach inorganic chemistry? Yes No * Are you able to teach physical chemistry? Yes No * What other courses are you interested in teaching? (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
