    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48675": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request when the application is submitted. Sam Houston State is a comprehensive University located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston. Current enrollment is approximately 21,500. Degrees conferred by the Department of Biological Sciences include a Bachelor of Science and Bachelor of Arts in Biology, a Bachelor of Science in Biomedical Sciences, and a Master of Science in Biology. The department is working to develop a Bachelor of Science in Forensic Biology and currently offers an interdisciplinary master’s degree in Forensic Science with the Departments of Criminal Justice and Chemistry. There are currently 23 full-time faculty, 5 full-time instructional staff, and 5 full-time staff members, including laboratory and teaching support staff and administrative support staff within the department. The Department of Biological Sciences is located in the newly built, state-of-the-art Life Sciences Building. The department is equipped to support broad research interests with facilities including small animal (e.g., rodent) housing that meets all current USDA standards, a microscopy suite with TEM, SEM, laser scanning, and confocal microscopes managed by a full-time PhD-level staff member, a molecular core with sequencing and imaging capabilities, and common use areas housing autoclaves, purified water systems, centrifuges, and other equipment to conduct cellular and molecular-based research. The department also maintains a 250-acre field station for teaching and research purposes that is equipped with a fully functional laboratory/classroom building. The field station is home to the Southeast Texas Applied Forensic Science (STAFS) facility, a state-of-the-art research, education, and training center designed to advance academic and technical knowledge in the application of anthropology, human anatomy, forensic science, biology, and chemistry. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Requisition 202600122F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Biological Sciences Open Date 09/21/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48579 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Christopher Randle Title Department Chair, Department of Biological Sciences, Box 2116, Huntsville, TX 77341-2116 Contact Phone 9365812117 Contact Email randle@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Biological Sciences in the College of Science and Engineering Technology at Sam Houston State University seeks a broadly trained biologist to support our Forensic Biology program for a tenure track faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor. Teaching responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, courses in Forensic Biology, General Biology, in addition to upper-level undergraduate, as well as graduate, courses in the candidate’s specific area of expertise. Educational Requirements for the Position The successful candidate will have earned a B.S. and a Doctoral degree in Life Sciences or a closely related field (Forensic Sciences, Physical Anthropology, Molecular Biology). Postdoctoral research experience is preferred but not required. Experience Required for the Position Candidates should have research experience beyond graduate study, preferably including one or more years of post-doctoral research. Other Requirements for the Position Area of research is open, but those with interests in Forensic Biology, Forensic Genetics, or Biological Anthropology are strongly encouraged to apply. The successful candidate will be required to develop an externally funded research program involving undergraduates and masters-level graduate students in addition to conducting collaborative research within the Department of Biological Sciences. Special Instructions Summary References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request when the application is submitted. Sam Houston State is a comprehensive University located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston. Current enrollment is approximately 21,500. Degrees conferred by the Department of Biological Sciences include a Bachelor of Science and Bachelor of Arts in Biology, a Bachelor of Science in Biomedical Sciences, and a Master of Science in Biology. The department is working to develop a Bachelor of Science in Forensic Biology and currently offers an interdisciplinary master’s degree in Forensic Science with the Departments of Criminal Justice and Chemistry. There are currently 23 full-time faculty, 5 full-time instructional staff, and 5 full-time staff members, including laboratory and teaching support staff and administrative support staff within the department. The Department of Biological Sciences is located in the newly built, state-of-the-art Life Sciences Building. The department is equipped to support broad research interests with facilities including small animal (e.g., rodent) housing that meets all current USDA standards, a microscopy suite with TEM , SEM , laser scanning, and confocal microscopes managed by a full-time PhD-level staff member, a molecular core with sequencing and imaging capabilities, and common use areas housing autoclaves, purified water systems, centrifuges, and other equipment to conduct cellular and molecular-based research. The department also maintains a 250-acre field station for teaching and research purposes that is equipped with a fully functional laboratory/classroom building. The field station is home to the Southeast Texas Applied Forensic Science ( STAFS ) facility, a state-of-the-art research, education, and training center designed to advance academic and technical knowledge in the application of anthropology, human anatomy, forensic science, biology, and chemistry. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48673": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request when the application is submitted. Sam Houston State University is classified as an R2 research institution. It is located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston. Current enrollment is approximately 22,000. Degrees conferred by the Department of Biological Sciences include a Bachelor of Science and Bachelor of Arts in Biology, a Bachelor of Science in Biomedical Sciences, and both a Master of Science and Master of Arts in Biology. There are currently 25 full-time faculty members, 5 full-time instructional staff, and 4 full-time support staff. The Department of Biological Sciences is in the newly constructed, state-of-the-art Life Sciences Building, which is well equipped to support research in parasitology. Facilities include a dedicated microscopy suite featuring transmission electron (TEM), scanning electron (SEM), laser-scanning, Keyence, and confocal microscopes, supported by a full-time master’s-level staff scientist. Additional resources include a molecular core facility with sequencing and imaging capabilities, as well as shared-use areas equipped with autoclaves, purified water systems, centrifuges, and other research infrastructure. In addition, the university maintains a small-animal (e.g., rodent) housing facility that meets all current USDA standards and has received OLAW Assurance from the NIH. The department also maintains the Piney Woods Environmental Research Laboratory, a 250-acre field station dedicated to research and teaching and equipped with laboratory and classroom facilities. The Texas Invasive Species Institute is housed on campus and offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration for the successful candidate. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Biological Sciences Requisition 202600121F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Biological Sciences Open Date 09/21/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48566 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Christopher Randle Title Department Chair, Department of Biological Sciences, Box 2116, Huntsville, TX 77341-2116 Contact Phone 9362941554 Contact Email randle@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Biological Sciences in the College of Science and Engineering Technology at Sam Houston State University seeks an individual broadly trained in the field of Parasitology and/or Parasite Ecology for a tenure track faculty position at the level of Assistant Professor. Teaching responsibilities may include but are not limited to Parasitology, Invertebrate Zoology, Evolution introductory biology courses, and upper-level undergraduate and graduate courses in the candidate’s area of expertise. Educational Requirements for the Position The successful candidate must possess a Bachelor’s degree and a Doctoral degree in Life Sciences or a closely related field. Experience Required for the Position Candidates should have research experience beyond graduate study, preferably including one or more years of post-doctoral research. Other Requirements for the Position Candidates with expertise in basic and/or applied research in parasitology and/or parasite ecology are strongly encouraged to apply. Relevant research areas include, but are not limited to, taxonomy and systematics, host-parasite interactions, parasite biodiversity, disease ecology, wildlife health, and the direct and indirect effects of parasites on individuals, populations, communities, and ecosystems. The successful candidate will develop an externally funded research program that engages undergraduates and masters-level graduate students, while also fostering collaborative research within the Department of Biological Sciences. Special Instructions Summary References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request when the application is submitted. Sam Houston State University is classified as an R2 research institution. It is located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston. Current enrollment is approximately 22,000. Degrees conferred by the Department of Biological Sciences include a Bachelor of Science and Bachelor of Arts in Biology, a Bachelor of Science in Biomedical Sciences, and both a Master of Science and Master of Arts in Biology. There are currently 25 full-time faculty members, 5 full-time instructional staff, and 4 full-time support staff. The Department of Biological Sciences is in the newly constructed, state-of-the-art Life Sciences Building, which is well equipped to support research in parasitology. Facilities include a dedicated microscopy suite featuring transmission electron ( TEM ), scanning electron ( SEM ), laser-scanning, Keyence, and confocal microscopes, supported by a full-time master’s-level staff scientist. Additional resources include a molecular core facility with sequencing and imaging capabilities, as well as shared-use areas equipped with autoclaves, purified water systems, centrifuges, and other research infrastructure. In addition, the university maintains a small-animal (e.g., rodent) housing facility that meets all current USDA standards and has received OLAW Assurance from the NIH . The department also maintains the Piney Woods Environmental Research Laboratory, a 250-acre field station dedicated to research and teaching and equipped with laboratory and classroom facilities. The Texas Invasive Species Institute is housed on campus and offers opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration for the successful candidate. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48548": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Pool Faculty - Competency-Based Education Instruction in Criminal Justice (up to 12 positions to be filled)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Lecturer-Pool Faculty - Competency-Based Education Instruction in Criminal Justice (up to 12 positions to be filled) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Lecturer-Pool Faculty - Competency-Based Education Instruction in Criminal Justice (up to 12 positions to be filled) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty - Competency-Based Education Instruction in Criminal Justice (up to 12 positions to be filled) Requisition 202600106F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Criminal Justice Department College of Criminal Justice Open Date 08/03/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48100 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Brooke Nodeland Title Assistant Dean ben012@shsu.edu Contact Phone (936) 294-4270 Contact Email ben012@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Support the delivery of courses in a competency-based education ( CBE ) format for the Bachelor of Applied Arts and Sciences ( BAAS ) in Criminal Justice. CBE courses are fully online and designated to allow students to progress by demonstrating mastery of clearly defined competencies. Faculty serve as instructors of record and are responsible for evaluating student work; providing timely, individualized feedback; monitoring student progress; maintaining regular communication with students; and supporting learner persistence toward mastery of course competencies. Faculty participate in required training, collaborate with program leadership to ensure instructional quality and consistency, and contribute to the continuous improvement of the competency-based education program. This position is structured as a 9-month academic-year appointment with an anticipated 3-month summer appointment to support the continuous delivery of the competency-based education program. Faculty are expected to provide instruction across multiple entry points throughout the calendar year, including summer, to ensure consistent support for student learning and progression. Educational Requirements for the Position Master’s degree in criminal justice, criminology, or closely related field Experience Required for the Position Minimum of five years of professional experience in criminal justice or related field.Strong written communication and feedback skills. Experience with online learning environments (e.g. Blackboard) Other Requirements for the Position Experience with competency-based education or outcomes-based assessment Experience working with adult learners Experience with supervising, training, or mentoring professionals Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to teach during the day? Yes No * Are you available to teach during the evening? Yes No Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Transcripts Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
