    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48512": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice in Engineering Technology (Safety Management)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Practice in Engineering Technology (Safety Management) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Practice in Engineering Technology (Safety Management) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice in Engineering Technology (Safety Management) Requisition 202600118F Rank Assistant Professor of Practice FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with qualifications and experiences; nine months Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Engineering Technology Open Date 09/09/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48468 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Suleiman Obeidat - Committee Chair Title Sam Houston State University Department of Engineering Technology Box 2088 Huntsville TX 77341-2088 Contact Phone 936-294-1091 Contact Email smo036@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The ability to teach traditional and online courses in Safety Management and Engineering Technology is expected. The successful applicant will contribute to the continued growth and improvement of the Environmental Health & Safety Management program through curriculum development, enhancement of teaching and laboratory resources, student mentoring, department service and applied undergraduate projects. The applicant is also expected to support program assessment, accreditation activities, and industry engagement. Educational Requirements for the Position An earned Masters or Doctorate degree ( ABD candidates will also be considered) in Safety Management, Occupational Safety and Health, Industrial Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Applied Engineering, Engineering Technology, or a closely related field is preferred. Applicants should have expertise in occupational and industrial safety, including safety management, OSHA compliance, hazard identification and risk assessment, and workplace safety. The ability to teach courses in Safety Management and contribute to other Engineering Technology program areas, such as Construction Management, Engineering Technology, and Engineering Design Technology, is desirable. Candidates with broad industry experience and interdisciplinary technical expertise are strongly encouraged to apply. Excellent communication skills and a strong commitment to undergraduate education are required. Relevant industry and college-level teaching experience, as well as professional certifications such as CSP , ASP , CIH , or CHST , are preferred. Experience Required for the Position Other Requirements for the Position The Department of Engineering Technology at SHSU has 700+ majors and offers 40+ different Engineering Technology courses. The new academic building – Fred Pirkle Engineering Technology Center houses the faculty offices, classrooms, CAD / CAM , electronics, 3D printing, innovation, material testing, and alternative energy labs. The department also maintains the Westmoreland Engineering Technology Center and Annex A, B, and C buildings which house the virtual reality, safety, woodworking, metalworking, CNC , material testing, and fluid power labs. Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Reference Contact Information Transcripts Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48510": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management - 2 positions to be filled",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Construction Management - 2 positions to be filled Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Construction Management - 2 positions to be filled Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Those interested in the position should submit all application materials through PeopleAdmin. This includes the online application, letter of interest, curriculum vita, philosophy of teaching, statement of research & goals, transcripts of all university work, and three letters of recommendation addressed to Dr. Basith. Review of applications will begin March 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Construction Management - 2 positions to be filled Requisition 202600021F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with experience and education. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Engineering Technology Open Date 02/27/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/46384 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Iftekhar Basith Title Committee Chair Department of Engineering Technology Sam Houston State University Box 2088 Huntsville, TX 77341-2088 Contact Phone 936-294-4139 Contact Email iib002@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Seventy-five percent teaching, twenty-five percent research appointment with service activities required for promotion, merit-based pay raise, and tenure. Ability to teach traditional and online courses is expected. Desired areas of interest include construction documentation, cost estimating, scheduling, surveying, project management, construction materials, or other subjects related to residential, commercial, and industrial construction. Educational Requirements for the Position An earned Doctorate degree in Construction Management/Engineering/ Science/Technology, Building Construction/Science, Civil Engineering/Technology with construction emphasis, Architectural Engineering with construction emphasis, or other closely related fields. Candidates in the above fields with ABD will also be considered. Experience Required for the Position Excellent communication skills are required. Applicant must have a strong commitment to undergraduate education and interdisciplinary collaboration. Other Requirements for the Position The successful applicant will contribute to our growing undergraduate research program. The applicant is expected to help with improving the Construction Management program including further development of lab and teaching resources, curriculum development, and application for ABET . Special Instructions Summary Those interested in the position should submit all application materials through PeopleAdmin. This includes the online application, letter of interest, curriculum vita, philosophy of teaching, statement of research & goals, transcripts of all university work, and three letters of recommendation addressed to Dr. Basith. Review of applications will begin March 16, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HBCU Connect - Historical