ons of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Physician Assistant Studies and Athletic Training (2026-2027) Requisition 202600104F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Health Sciences Department Dept of Physician Assistants Open Date 08/04/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48028 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Wilma Mealer, Chair of MPAS Title Wilma Mealer, Chair of MPAS and AT at the Health Professions Building Conroe, TX Contact Phone 936-202-5539 Contact Email wjm026@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Lecturer-Pool Faculty will teach graduate courses within the Master of Physician Assistant Studies program, depending on an applicant’s academic background, experience, and licensure. Pool faculty contracts are for one semester based on departmental needs but may be renewed based on performance and need. Departmental need is driven by student enrollment and internal workload commitments. Educational Requirements for the Position All candidates should possess excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work effectively as a team member. Must have knowledge and the ability to comply with accreditation standards related to evaluation and assessment. Physician Assistant with the following: 1. Master’s degree from an ARC -PA accredited program. 2. Current NCCPA certification 3. Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience. 4. Current license or eligibility for licensing as a physician assistant in the State of Texas. OR Physician with the following: 1. A Doctor of Medicine/Osteopathy with a full unrestricted MD license or eligibility to obtain such licensure in the State of Texas. OR Non-clinician Scientist or Health Professional with the following: 1. Master’s degree or higher in a health or science related field. Experience Required for the Position The Lecturer-Pool Faculty will teach graduate courses within the Master of Physician Assistant Studies program, depending on an applicant’s academic background, experience, and licensure. Pool faculty contracts are for one semester based on departmental needs but may be renewed based on performance and need. Departmental need is driven by student enrollment and internal workload commitments. Other Requirements for the Position Special Instructions Summary Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas’ legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consort