    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48058": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Health Information Technology (HIT) - Up to 3 positions to be filled",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Health Information Technology (HIT) - Up to 3 positions to be filled Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Health Information Technology (HIT) - Up to 3 positions to be filled Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Health Information Technology (HIT) - Up to 3 positions to be filled Requisition 202600097F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College Polytechnic College Department Polytechnic College Open Date 07/30/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/47898 Refer Applicants To Contact Name James Harris Title Health Information Technology, Program Director Contact Phone (936)294-2213 Contact Email jrh093@SHSU.EDU Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Our Health Information Technology program prepares students for success in the rapidly growing healthcare industry through practical training, real-world application, career-ready skills, and an industry-aligned curriculum. We are seeking an experienced Health Information Management ( HIM ) or Health Information Technology ( HIT ) professional with a passion for preparing the next generation of healthcare professionals to teach online courses in our accelerated Health Information Technology program. Prepare students for immediate employment by delivering applied instruction focused on current healthcare practices, health information systems, regulatory compliance, and employer needs. Teach courses in our Health Information Technology program, helping students develop the knowledge and skills needed to manage health information, support healthcare operations, and ensure the accuracy, privacy, and security of patient data. Courses may include Health Information Systems, Medical Terminology, Health Data Content and Structure, Legal and Ethical Aspects of Health Information, Health Care Delivery Systems, Coding and Reimbursement Methodologies, Advanced Medical Coding, Quality Assessment and Performance Improvement, RHIT (Registered Health Information Technician) Competency Review, and related Health Information Technology courses, depending on the selected candidate’s expertise and program needs. This is a part-time online position, ideal for working health information professionals who want to share their expertise and experience with future Health Information Technology professionals. Educational Requirements for the Position Bachelor’s degree in Health Information Management, Health Information Technology, Health Administration, Healthcare Informatics, or a closely related field. Master’s degree strongly preferred. Current RHIA (Registered Health Information Administrator) or RHIT (Registered Health Information Technician) credential preferred. Additional industry certifications (e.g., CCS , CCS -P, CPC , CHDA , CHPS , CDIP ) are desirable depending on the candidate’s area of expertise. Experience Required for the Position Professional experience in Health Information Management, Health Information Technology, medical coding, clinical documentation improvement, healthcare compliance, health data analytics, electronic health record systems, or a related healthcare field. Previous teaching or training experience is preferred. Strong commitment to the mission of the SHSU Polytechnic College. Demonstrated knowledge of health information management principles, healthcare regulations, coding systems, electronic health records, privacy and security standards, and healthcare reimbursement. Excellent communication, organizational, and interpersonal skills. Experience with online learning platforms (e.g., Blackboard) is preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Preferred qualifications include familiarity with, or willingness to adopt, best practices for online teaching and learning, including the effective use of Blackboard. Demonstrated commitment to quality instruction, student success, career readiness, and workforce development. Ability to integrate current healthcare technologies and industry practices into instruction. Ability to establish and maintain positive and effective working relationships with students, faculty, staff, healthcare partners, and the public. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing; analyze information, solve problems, and present complex healthcare concepts in an accessible manner. Strong attention to detail, organizational skills, and ability to manage multiple responsibilities with minimal supervision. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a student-centered, customer-service-oriented environment. Applicants must be able to demonstrate fluency in written and spoken English. Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to teach during the day? Yes No * Are you available to teach during the evening? Yes No Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
