ployer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Criminal Justice and Criminology in Fall 2026, Spring 2027/Summer 2027 (up to 5 positions to be filled) Requisition 202600030F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Criminal Justice Department Dept of Criminal Justice and Criminology Open Date 03/09/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/46537 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Wanda Leal Title Assistant Department Chair College of Criminal Justice Sam Houston State University Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone (936) 294-1667 Contact Email wel004@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Lecturer-pool faculty are term positions hired to teach 1-4 courses per semester. Hiring is based on student demand on a semester-by-semester basis. The instructor is responsible for teaching a wide range of courses to support the department degree programs. Educational Requirements for the Position JD or Master’s Degree in Criminal Justice or closely related field. Experience Required for the Position Relevant teaching and/or practical experience. Other Requirements for the Position Applicants should submit with the application: vitae, three (3) reference letters, and unofficial transcripts. Special Instructions Summary Responsible for teaching a wide range of courses to support the Department of Criminal Justice and Criminology’s undergraduate and graduate degree programs This posting is for Fall 2026, Spring 2027 & Summer 2027 Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disab