    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/44347": {
      "title": "Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Kinesiology - Up to 5 positions to be filled (2026)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Kinesiology - Up to 5 positions to be filled (2026) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Kinesiology - Up to 5 positions to be filled (2026) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU includes a faculty, students, and staff with various experiences and backgrounds ( https://www.shsu.edu/academics/health-sciences/about-the-college/faculty_staff_contacts.html#kinesiology ). The department offers a five (5) undergraduate degrees or tracks and three (3) graduate degrees ( https://www.shsu.edu/academics/health-sciences/kinesiology/ ). The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU seeks to recruit and retain qualified faculty. Qualified applicants with experience working in different settings and/or who demonstrate a commitment to serving various student populations are strongly encouraged to apply. There are multiple options for places to live near our multiple campuses. Sam Houston’s main campus is located in Huntsville, TX. The city of Huntsville is nestled in the East Texas Piney Woods and is centrally located on a direct route between Houston and Dallas. With a population of roughly 40,000 (excluding SHSU), Huntsville offers the simplicity of small-town life and easy access to surrounding larger cities including Conroe (where the College of Osteopathic Medicine is located), The Woodlands (where the School of Nursing and The Woodlands Center is located), and Bryan/College Station. Full of Texas history and charm, this county seat is home to multiple museums, annual festivities, antique stores, year-round outdoor activities, vineyards, golf courses, lakes, and a beautiful state park. In a little over an hour after leaving main campus, you can arrive in downtown Houston. It provides access to large entertainment venues and professional sporting events. If you prefer life on the water, Lake Conroe and Lake Livingston are a short commute, and Galveston Island and the Gulf coast are a two-hour drive. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Lecturer-Pool Faculty of Kinesiology - Up to 5 positions to be filled (2026) Requisition 202500103F Rank Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Health Sciences Department Dept of Kinesiology Open Date 07/29/2023 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/44234 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Destiny Rice Title Administrative Associate II Contact Phone 936-294-1398 Contact Email dcd024@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Lecturer-Pool Faculty will teach undergraduate or graduate courses within one or more of the Department of Kinesiology degree programs, dependent upon an applicant’s academic background, experience, and licensure. Pool faculty contracts are for one semester based on departmental needs but may be renewed based on performance and need. Departmental need is driven by student enrollment and internal workload commitments. Please indicate your area(s) of academic and professional expertise when applying. Areas to select from include: a) Athletic Training b) Coaching c) Exercise Science d) Motor Behavior e) Sport Management f) Sport Psychology/Sociology. Educational Requirements for the Position Master’s degree from an accredited institution in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Athletic Training, Sport Management or a related field for lower-level course offerings. Doctoral degree preferred from an accredited institution in Kinesiology, Exercise Science, Athletic Training, Sport Management or a related field for graduate course offerings. Candidates must have their degree completed by their contract start date. Experience Required for the Position Professional experience and/or certifications in the specific area is preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Minimum of three (3) years of teaching experience is preferred. Travel to SHSU Campuses in Huntsville, TX, Conroe, TX, and/or The Woodlands, TX are required for some positions, typically 2-3 days/week. Experience in online teaching and online training and certificates required for those who will teach online courses. Certifications ( ATC ) and Licensure ( LAT ) are required for those teaching in the MSAT program. Special Instructions Summary The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU includes a faculty, students, and staff with various experiences and backgrounds ( https://www.shsu.edu/academics/health-sciences/about-the-college/faculty_staff_contacts.html#kinesiology ). The department offers a five (5) undergraduate degrees or tracks and three (3) graduate degrees ( https://www.shsu.edu/academics/health-sciences/kinesiology/ ). The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU seeks to recruit and retain qualified faculty. Qualified applicants with experience working in different settings and/or who demonstrate a commitment to serving various student populations are strongly encouraged to apply. There are multiple options for places to live near our multiple campuses. Sam Houston’s main campus is located in Huntsville, TX. The city of Huntsville is nestled in the East Texas Piney Woods and is centrally located on a direct route between Houston and Dallas. With a population of roughly 40,000 (excluding SHSU ), Huntsville offers the simplicity of small-town life and easy access to surrounding larger cities including Conroe (where the College of Osteopathic Medicine is located), The Woodlands (where the School of Nursing and The Woodlands Center is located), and Bryan/College Station. Full of Texas history and charm, this county seat is home to multiple museums, annual festivities, antique stores, year-round outdoor activities, vineyards, golf courses, lakes, and a beautiful state park. In a little over an hour after leaving main campus, you can arrive in downtown Houston. It provides access to large entertainment venues and professional sporting events. If you prefer life on the water, Lake Conroe and Lake Livingston are a short commute, and Galveston Island and the Gulf coast are a two-hour drive. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HBCU Connect - Historically Black Colleges and Universities HACU - Hispanic Association of Colleges & Universities The Journal of Blacks in Higher Education Association for Women in Science TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee SHSU Recruiter Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) * Are you available to teach during the day? Yes No * Please indicate your teaching availability. Face-to-Face Only Online Only Face-to-Face and Online * Are you available to teach during the evening? Yes No Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
