alary Commensurate with experience and education. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Science & Engineering Technology Department Dept of Chemistry Open Date 10/26/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48906 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Dustin E. Gross Title Department of Chemistry Sam Houston State University Box 2117 Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-1532 Contact Email Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Lecturer in Chemistry is expected to teach organic chemistry, as well as other chemistry courses as needed and consistent with the candidate’s expertise. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence through innovative, inclusive, and evidence-based instructional practices. The lecturer will design and maintain high-quality course materials, provide timely and constructive feedback to students, and hold regular office hours to support academic success. They are expected to contribute to curriculum improvement and collaborate effectively with colleagues to advance departmental goals. Active participation in service, advising, and professional development to enhance teaching and promote student engagement is also expected. Educational Requirements for the Position A Ph.D. in Chemistry is preferred, although a Master’s degree with 18 graduate hours of chemistry would be considered. Experience Required for the Position Other Requirements for the Position Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Special Instructions Summary Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Review of application materials will begin November 13, 2026. The position will begin January 16, 2027. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke