    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49030": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Physician Assistant Studies - MPAS Program (2 positions)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Physician Assistant Studies - MPAS Program (2 positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Physician Assistant Studies - MPAS Program (2 positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Physician Assistant Studies - MPAS Program (2 positions) Requisition 202600119F Rank Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Health Sciences Department Dept of Physician Assistants Open Date 09/22/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48454 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Prof. Wilma Mealer Title Department Chair, Physician Assistant Studies and Athletic Training Contact Phone 936-202-5539 Contact Email wjm026@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The College of Health Sciences at Sam Houston State University ( SHSU ) is pleased to invite qualified applications for an Instructional Faculty position at the Clinical Assistant/Associate/Full Professor rank (12-month appointment) in the proposed Master of Physician Assistant Studies ( MPAS ) Program. The Instructional Faculty will report to the Program Director and work closely with other MPAS faculty and staff to support the program’s mission and maintain compliance with ARC -PA accreditation standards. Primary responsibilities include providing student instruction and teaching courses (didactic and/or clinical as assigned by the Program Director). The selected candidate will be responsible for administrative duties, including participating in the admission process, scheduling clinical rotations, and assisting the clinical team with program evaluation during the clinical phase. Duties will also include maintaining data and assessments to prepare reports for accreditation purposes. The faculty will be responsible for academic mentoring and advising of learners. The selected candidate will assist the Clinical Coordinator in delivering classroom learning experiences and clinical skills instruction on essential medical and clinical science topics, tailored to the individual’s qualifications. Collaboration with the Department Chair, Director of the MPAS Program, Medical Director, and other principal faculty members will be necessary to manage the curriculum effectively and ensure high-quality instruction. Educational Requirements for the Position Physician Assistant - Master’s degree from an ARC -PA accredited program. OR Physician – A Doctor of Medicine/Osteopathy Experience Required for the Position All candidates should possess excellent oral, written, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to work effectively as a team member. Must have knowledge and the ability to comply with accreditation standards related to evaluation and assessment. Physician Assistant with the following: Master’s degree from an ARC -PA accredited program. Minimum of 2 years of clinical experience. Current license or eligibility for licensing as a physician assistant in the State of Texas. OR Physician with the following: A Doctor of Medicine/Osteopathy with a full unrestricted MD license or eligibility to obtain such licensure in the State of Texas. OR Non-clinician Scientist or Health Professional with the following: Master’s degree or higher in a health- or science-related field. Other Requirements for the Position The selected candidate will maintain awareness of the PA profession and participate in service to the program, university, and healthcare profession. The MPAS Program at SHSU seeks faculty with strong teaching, clinical, scholarly, and service backgrounds. Candidates with experience teaching, mentoring, and advising students in higher education and professional healthcare programs are encouraged to apply. The SHSU student body comprises over 50% first-generation college students. Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Reference Contact Information Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49023": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer in Criminal Justice &amp; Criminology (2 positions)",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer in Criminal Justice &amp; Criminology (2 positions) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer in Criminal Justice & Criminology (2 positions) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted online and should include a letter of interest, a current vita, teaching philosophy, and reference contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the search process. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer in Criminal Justice & Criminology (2 positions) Requisition 202600137F Rank Assistant Professor of Practice or Lecturer FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Criminal Justice Department Dept of Criminal Justice and Criminology Open Date 10/23/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48948 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Jason Ingram Title Chair, Criminal Justice & Criminology, College of Criminal Justice, SHSU , Huntsville, TX 77341-2296 Contact Phone (936) 294-1698 Contact Email jri004@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Teach four (4) classes each semester of undergraduate and/or graduate courses delivered face-to-face and/or online: (15-week, 7.5 weeks, or 5-week terms) at main campus based on departmental needs. This is an in-person position with on-campus presence expectations. This position also has department, college, and university service expectations. Educational Requirements for the Position The successful candidate must have a terminal degree, such as a J.D. or Ph.D., in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related academic field. Experience Required for the Position Preference will be given to candidates who have experience as a criminal justice professional and/or who have proficiency in teaching criminal justice courses (college or university). Other Requirements for the Position Successful candidate will receive a nine-month contract and be eligible for a summer contract. Work may require evenings and weekends. Special Instructions Summary To ensure full consideration, applications must be submitted online and should include a letter of interest, a current vita, teaching philosophy, and reference contact information. Letters of recommendation may be requested at a later stage of the search process. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Reference Contact Information Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
