    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49016": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sport Management",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Sport Management Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Sport Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested candidates must submit the following required documents: Cover letter detailing candidate’s interest in the position, teaching experience in sport management, research interests and proposed five-year research agenda, involvement in service at the community, departmental, university, state or national level, and sport industry experience; it is also recommended that a candidate address any experiences related to the preferred criteria listed in the position description. Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin September 2026. Position will start January 2027 or until filled. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Sport Management Requisition 202600075F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Health Sciences Department Dept of Kinesiology Open Date 06/11/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/47440 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Deven Merchant Title Assistant to the Chair, Kinesiology 1900 Avenue I Suite 107E Huntsville, TX 77340 Contact Phone 936-294-2266 Contact Email dmerchant@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU invites applications for a nine month, full-time, tenure-track, Assistant Professor of Sport Management with the possibility of summer employment based on student need and enrollment (summer is not guaranteed). Currently, the department offers a hybrid (face-to-face and online) 36-hour Master of Science degree program with both thesis and practicum options. The successful candidate will also assist in the implementation of a new undergraduate degree program in Sport Management (pending final approval). The duties and responsibilities of this position include: Teaching: teaching assignments may include undergraduate ( taught at main campus in Huntsville, TX) and graduate (taught in the evenings at The Woodlands Center located in The Woodlands, TX) coursework (both face-to-face and online). Research: maintaining a research agenda in Sport Management and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students in research and professional development. Service: performing university and professional service and contributing to ongoing program evaluation and improvement in the undergraduate and graduate programs within the department. Educational Requirements for the Position An earned doctorate from an accredited institution in Sport Management/Administration or related discipline is required ( ABD candidates considered). ABD candidates must have doctoral degree conferred by start date. Experience Required for the Position Teaching experience in sport management/administration. A demonstrated record of research and scholarship in the field. Sport industry work experience. An established network in the sport industry. Active membership in professional organizations related to the field Other Requirements for the Position The Department of Kinesiology at SHSU includes faculty, students, and staff from a variety of backgrounds, experiences, and skills https://www.shsu.edu/academics/colleges/health-sciences/kinesiology/people . Currently, the department offers BS degrees in Human Performance and Wellness Management, Clinical Exercise Science, Clinical Exercise Science 3+2 to Masters in Athletic Training ( MSAT ), Physical Education Teacher Education (double major), Sport Management (pending final approval this summer) and Kinesiology; and MS degrees in Kinesiology-Sport and Human Performance and Sport Management; and minors in Sport Coaching and Kinesiology ( https://www.shsu.edu/academics/colleges/health-sciences/kinesiology/programs ) . (watch this virtual tour https://youtu.be/-nCkTSgvI4Y ) There are multiple options for places to live near our multiple campuses. Sam Houston’s main campus is located in Huntsville. The city of Huntsville is nestled in the East Texas Piney Woods and is centrally located on a direct route between Houston and Dallas. With a population of roughly 40,000 (excluding SHSU ), Huntsville offers the simplicity of small-town life and easy access to surrounding larger cities including Conroe ,where both the College of Osteopathic Medicine and the new Health Professions Buildings ( HPB ) are located (the HPB houses the Masters in Physician Assistant Studies, MSAT , MS in Dietetics, and the proposed Doctor in Physical Therapy), The Woodlands, where the School of Nursing and The Woodlands Center ( TWC ) is located, and Bryan/College Station. Full of Texas history and charm, this county seat is home to multiple museums, annual festivities, antique stores, year-round outdoor activities, vineyards, golf courses, lakes, and a beautiful state park. In a little over an hour after leaving the main campus, you can arrive in downtown Houston. Houston has a variety of amenities to offer and is considered one of the best “foodie” cities. This city also provides access to large entertainment venues and professional sporting events. If you prefer life on the water, Lake Conroe and Lake Livingston are a short commute, and Galveston Island and the Gulf coast are a two-hour drive from Huntsville. Special Instructions Summary Interested candidates must submit the following required documents: Cover letter detailing candidate’s interest in the position, teaching experience in sport management, research interests and proposed five-year research agenda, involvement in service at the community, departmental, university, state or national level, and sport industry experience; it is also recommended that a candidate address any experiences related to the preferred criteria listed in the position description. Curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three professional references Review of applications will begin September 2026. Position will start January 2027 or until filled. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Optional Documents Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Transcripts Teaching Evaluations © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49066": {
      "title": "Program Director, Paralegal Studies/Assistant Professor of Practice",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Program Director, Paralegal Studies/Assistant Professor of Practice Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Program Director, Paralegal Studies/Assistant Professor of Practice Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Sam Houston State University is a university located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston, with an enrolment of about 22,000 students. The Polytechnic College is the newest college at Sam Houston State University, with a mission to meet the needs of industry for high-skill employees. The SHSU Polytechnic College offers industry-aligned workforce/technical educational programs that result in lower-level credentials (certificates and associate degrees), providing students with industry-aligned skills required for successful employment in high-demand occupations throughout the SHSU service area (Greater Houston and Southeast Texas). The college engages a large network of industry partners to ensure a contemporary and practical curriculum that generates high-quality employment opportunities for graduates. The successful candidate will inherit an operating program with enrolled students, graduates, adjunct instructors, employer relationships, and an established curriculum. The Program Director will be expected to strengthen the program’s academic quality, enrollment, student support, employer engagement, work-based learning opportunities, graduate placement, and pathways to continued education. Interested applicants should apply online. Review of applications will begin on 25 NOV 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Program Director, Paralegal Studies/Assistant Professor of Practice Requisition 202600140F Rank Assistant Professor of Practice FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College Polytechnic College Department Polytechnic College Open Date 10/27/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49000 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Clayton Cottle Title Assistant Vice President for Operations & Administration Contact Phone 9362943119 Contact Email cottle@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Program Director of Paralegal Studies, in collaboration with Polytechnic College leadership, provides the academic, operational, and instructional leadership necessary to advance the mission and continued growth of the Paralegal Studies Program. The program is delivered fully online through an accelerated format and offers a stackable Level I Certificate and Associate of Applied Science degree. The Program Director is responsible for maintaining a high-quality, workforce-aligned curriculum that prepares students for employment and career advancement in law firms, government agencies, corporate legal departments, and other legal environments. The Program Director leads the program’s day-to-day academic operations, including curriculum development and review, course scheduling, instructional assignments, faculty recruitment and onboarding, program assessment, budget management, and coordination with college and university offices. The Director works closely with employers, legal professionals, advisory committee members, and community partners to ensure that curriculum and student experiences remain aligned with workforce needs. The Program Director, in collaboration with Polytechnic College leadership, supports enrollment, retention, completion, and graduate employment by collaborating with admissions, advising, financial aid, the Registrar, career services, and other student-support offices. The Director also develops and maintains internships, cooperative education opportunities, employer partnerships, and pathways that allow certificate and AAS completers to continue their education, including applicable BAAS and transfer opportunities. This is a faculty position with administrative responsibilities. The Program Director maintains an instructional assignment, with appropriate administrative workload recognition, and must be able to teach effectively in an online, accelerated learning environment. Educational Requirements for the Position Candidates must meet at least one of the following qualification standards: Master’s degree or higher in the teaching discipline; Master’s degree in another discipline with at least 18 graduate semester credit hours in the teaching discipline; Bachelor’s degree in the teaching discipline; Bachelor’s degree in another discipline with at least 12 undergraduate semester credit hours in the teaching discipline or a related field; or Associate degree in the teaching discipline and at least three years of relevant full-time professional experience. A Juris Doctor or a master’s degree in paralegal studies, legal studies, or a closely related field is preferred. Experience Required for the Position Relevant professional experience in a legal or paralegal setting is required. Candidates must possess the professional knowledge necessary to develop, deliver, and assess curriculum that prepares students for employment in the legal profession. Demonstrated teaching or training experience in paralegal studies, legal studies, law, or a related field in a postsecondary or professional setting is required. The following experience is preferred: teaching and developing courses for online or accelerated delivery. Developing and assessing student learning outcomes. Leading or administering an academic, workforce, training, or professional program. Recruiting, onboarding, supporting, and evaluating full-time or adjunct instructors. Developing employer partnerships, internships, cooperative education placements, or other work-based learning opportunities. Supporting student recruitment, persistence, completion, and employment. Using enrollment, student-success, and workforce-outcome data to guide program decisions. Working with Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board requirements and workforce-education curriculum processes; and working with learning-management systems, preferably Blackboard. Other Requirements for the Position Program Leadership and Administration Provide strategic and operational leadership for the Paralegal Studies Program. Develop and maintain program goals, annual priorities, enrollment targets, and student-success objectives in collaboration with college leadership. Develop course schedules and instructional assignments that support student progression through accelerated parts of term. Recruit, onboard, mentor, coordinate, and evaluate instructors. Promote communication and consistency across courses and instructors. Identify instructional, technology, staffing, and professional-development needs. Address student, faculty, and program concerns in a timely, constructive, and student-centered manner. Maintain accurate program records and complete required institutional reports and documentation. Curriculum, Instruction, and Assessment Teach courses in the Paralegal Studies Program. Develop and maintain rigorous, practical, and workforce-aligned course content. Ensure consistency in course expectations, learning outcomes, instructional materials, and assessment practices across instructors and course sections. Coordinate the development and maintenance of syllabi, master course materials, assignments, assessments, and instructional media. Review and revise curriculum in response to changes in the legal profession, technology, employer expectations, and applicable state and institutional requirements. Lead program review, annual assessment, and evaluation of student learning outcomes. Apply effective practices for teaching and supporting adult learners, working professionals, first-generation students, and students in an accelerated online environment. Support accessible, engaging, and effective use of educational technology. Student Success and Enrollment Serve as a primary source of program-specific academic advising and mentoring for Paralegal Studies students. Work with appropriate university offices to support prospective and current students from inquiry through application, enrollment, completion, and employment. Contribute subject-matter expertise to recruitment, outreach, and program-marketing efforts. Monitor enrollment, course success, persistence, certificate and degree completion, and other program indicators. Provide or coordinate timely academic guidance and high-touch student support. Identify barriers affecting student progress and work collaboratively to develop practical interventions. Support clear pathways from the Level I Certificate into the AAS and from the AAS into applicable BAAS or other continuing-education opportunities. Employer Partnerships and Graduate Outcomes Maintain an active employer advisory committee and engage legal professionals in ongoing program improvement. Develop relationships with law firms, courts, government agencies, corporate legal departments, nonprofit organizations, and other prospective employers. Expand internships, cooperative education placements, mentorships, guest instruction, and other work-based learning opportunities. Collaborate with career services and college personnel to support placement of graduates into appropriate legal-support positions. Assist in tracking and evaluating internship participation, graduate employment, employer feedback, and other workforce outcomes. Represent the program at professional, community, recruitment, and employer-engagement events. Compliance and Collaboration Maintain compliance with applicable university, Texas Higher Education Coordinating Board, institutional accreditation, and professional requirements. Support preparation for and maintenance of any specialized program recognition or approval pursued by the college. Collaborate effectively with Polytechnic College leadership, faculty, staff, and university offices. Demonstrate sound judgment, integrity, adaptability, clear communication, and a commitment to collaborative problem-solving. Perform other related duties as assigned. Special Instructions Summary Sam Houston State University is a university located in East Texas, approximately 65 miles north of Houston, with an enrolment of about 22,000 students. The Polytechnic College is the newest college at Sam Houston State University, with a mission to meet the needs of industry for high-skill employees. The SHSU Polytechnic College offers industry-aligned workforce/technical educational programs that result in lower-level credentials (certificates and associate degrees), providing students with industry-aligned skills required for successful employment in high-demand occupations throughout the SHSU service area (Greater Houston and Southeast Texas). The college engages a large network of industry partners to ensure a contemporary and practical curriculum that generates high-quality employment opportunities for graduates. The successful candidate will inherit an operating program with enrolled students, graduates, adjunct instructors, employer relationships, and an established curriculum. The Program Director will be expected to strengthen the program’s academic quality, enrollment, student support, employer engagement, work-based learning opportunities, graduate placement, and pathways to continued education. Interested applicants should apply online. Review of applications will begin on 25 NOV 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Letter of Recommendation 1 Letter of Recommendation 2 Letter of Recommendation 3 Transcripts Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
