    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49065": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Medicine - 4 Positions to be Filled",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Medicine - 4 Positions to be Filled Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Medicine - 4 Positions to be Filled Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Medicine - 4 Positions to be Filled Requisition 202500023F Rank Assistant or Associate Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with experience and education. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Non-Tenure Track College Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine Department Dept of Primary Care and Clinical Medicine Open Date 03/10/2025 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/42742 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Kathryn Potter Title 925 City Central Ave Conroe, TX 77304 936-202-5226 Contact Phone (936)202-5233 Contact Email kpotter@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Serves the Sam Houston State University Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine ( SHSU - GCOM ) in the Department of Primary Care and Clinical Medicine. The University is seeking qualified candidates to join SHSU - GCOM as full-time Clinical Faculty. The position reports to the Chair of Primary Care and Clinical Medicine. The University is focused on improving the physician workforce in primary care and other specialties identified as a physician shortage in the State of Texas and has developed an integrated curriculum merging basic science instruction with clinical learning and an osteopathic emphasis. The Clinical Faculty member will be expected to act as mentors, particularly for students wishing to practice in primary care fields or in rural/community-based medicine. The clinical faculty members will assist the Chair of Primary Care and Clinical Medicine in development of clinical content for systems courses and clerkships. Participate in scholarship and research in the department, provide quality patient care and foster collaboration and interdisciplinary learning. Members of the Department of Primary Care and Clinical Medicine will be expected to participate in teaching in the systems courses, physical exam course, case-based learning sessions, clinical clerkships, procedural skills training, OSCE’s and (where appropriate) Osteopathic Manipulative Medicine hands on training. Individuals should be comfortable working in preclinical and clinical education, as well as evaluation of curriculum and students through various learning and assessment methods. Where appropriate, the members of the department will participate in the SHSU faculty practice in the SHSU Physicians clinic. However, there may be opportunities for members of the clinical faculty to be granted part-time contracts with SHSU in order to provide patient care with external clinical practices. Further, in some cases, consideration for full or part-time faculty contracts may be considered for clinicians who are no longer practicing medicine. Please note this position is located in Conroe at the Sam Houston State University Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine facility. Educational Requirements for the Position The successful candidate will have a DO or MD degree from a College of Osteopathic or Allopathic Medicine with successful completion of residency training, current AOA or ABMS board certification or board eligibility, a current unrestricted license to practice in Texas (or eligibility to obtain a medical license in Texas). Preference will be given to primary care physicians with training and experience in osteopathic manipulative medicine, however physicians with any degree or specialty will be considered. If a successful candidate does not possess an active license to practice medicine in Texas, the position will commence once an unrestricted license to practice medicine in Texas is obtained. Experience Required for the Position This position requires clinical skills and well-developed communication skills. A background in medical education is preferred, as is experience in pre-clinical and clinical teaching. Those able to teach osteopathic manipulative medicine preferred but not required. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with experience and training. Other Requirements for the Position Ability to communicate and work with faculty, medical students, clerkship coordinators, hospital administrators, physician preceptors and college administration. Excellent written and verbal communication. Demonstrates personal initiative and abilities to deal with a rapidly changing environment. Familiarity with Learning Management Systems and reporting is preferred. Other duties as assigned. Special Instructions Summary Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Education HBCU Connect - Historically Black Colleges and Universities HACU - Hispanic Association of Colleges & Universities The Journal of Blacks in Higher Education Association for Women in Science TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee SHSU Recruiter Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49100": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Public Health",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant Professor of Public Health Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant Professor of Public Health Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. AI Statement: Application materials, including cover letter and the statements of teaching philosophy and research, should be written by the applicant. Generative AI tools may be used for grammatical proofreading only. Please do not use AI to draft, write, or substantially revise any portion of your application. The Department of Public Health at Sam Houston State University is part of the College of Health Sciences and is home to a dedicated team of faculty, staff, and students. We offer a range of undergraduate and graduate programs designed to prepare students for impactful careers in public health. Visit our website to learn more about our team and explore our academic programs: https://www.shsu.edu/academics/colleges/health-sciences/public-health/# . Location and Lifestyle: There are multiple options for places to live near our different campuses. Sam Houston’s main campus is located in Huntsville, Texas. The city of Huntsville is nestled in the East Texas Piney Woods and is centrally located on a direct route between Houston and Dallas. With a population of roughly 48,550 (excluding SHSU), Huntsville offers the simplicity of small-town life and easy access to surrounding larger cities including Conroe (where the Russell and Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine and the Health Professions Building are located), The Woodlands (where the School of Nursing and The Woodlands Center is located), and Bryan/College Station. The Texas Medical Center, located in Houston, is the largest medical center in the world and is a 75-mile drive from Huntsville. Huntsville is full of Texas history and charm, and this county seat is home to multiple museums, annual festivities, antique stores, year-round outdoor activities, vineyards, golf courses, lakes, and a beautiful state park. In a little over an hour after leaving main campus, you can arrive in downtown Houston. It provides access to large entertainment venues and professional sporting events. If you prefer life on the water, Lake Conroe and Lake Livingston are a short commute, and Galveston Island and the Gulf coast are a two-hour drive. A quick 35-minute drive down I-45 South takes you to The Woodlands, which offers 220 miles of hike and bike trails,150 parks to enjoy, and easy access to numerous shopping, sport, and dining venues. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant Professor of Public Health Requisition 202600143F Rank Assistant Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College College of Health Sciences Department Dept of Public Health Open Date 10/29/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49031 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Dr. Rosanne Keathley Title Associate Chair Department of Public Health, Sam Houston State University PO Box 2194 Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone 936-294-1171 Contact Email hpe_rsk@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Public Health at Sam Houston State University invites applications for a full-time, 9- month, tenure track Assistant Professor of Public Health. Candidates with expertise in epidemiology are strongly preferred. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Public Health, including epidemiology and other courses aligned with the candidate’s expertise and departmental needs. The position carries a 3/3 teaching load and requires a regular on-campus presence in Huntsville; teaching assignments may include face-to-face and online format. The faculty member will maintain an active program of scholarship, pursue external funding as appropriate, and contribute service to the department, college, university, and profession. Responsibilities also include advising and mentoring students; supporting experiential learning and community-engaged opportunities; developing relationships with public health agencies, health care providers, and community organizations; and participating in assessment, accreditation, and program review. Other duties may be assigned. Educational Requirements for the Position An earned doctoral degree (PhD, DrPH, or equivalent) in public health or a closely related field is required by the appointment start date. ABD candidates may be considered if the doctorate will be completed by September 1, 2027. Degrees from international institutions must be equivalent to the required doctoral degree. Experience Required for the Position Candidates with research and/or teaching experience in epidemiology are strongly preferred. Research experience in biostatistics or a closely related public health field will also be considered. Qualified applicants should demonstrate evidence of scholarly activity through peer-reviewed publications, grant activity, research collaborations, or other scholarly contributions. Applicants with a minimum of one peer-reviewed publication are preferred. Professional or applied experience in public health or a related field is also preferred. Applicants are required to have a minimum of one year teaching experience at the undergraduate or graduate level in an institution of higher education. Experience with program assessment, accreditation, or program review is also recommended. Other Requirements for the Position Maintain excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service to the department and university. Performs other duties as requested or assigned by the administration. Special Instructions Summary Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. AI Statement: Application materials, including cover letter and the statements of teaching philosophy and research, should be written by the applicant. Generative AI tools may be used for grammatical proofreading only. Please do not use AI to draft, write, or substantially revise any portion of your application. The Department of Public Health at Sam Houston State University is part of the College of Health Sciences and is home to a dedicated team of faculty, staff, and students. We offer a range of undergraduate and graduate programs designed to prepare students for impactful careers in public health. Visit our website to learn more about our team and explore our academic programs: https://www.shsu.edu/academics/colleges/health-sciences/public-health/# . Location and Lifestyle: There are multiple options for places to live near our different campuses. Sam Houston’s main campus is located in Huntsville, Texas. The city of Huntsville is nestled in the East Texas Piney Woods and is centrally located on a direct route between Houston and Dallas. With a population of roughly 48,550 (excluding SHSU ), Huntsville offers the simplicity of small-town life and easy access to surrounding larger cities including Conroe (where the Russell and Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine and the Health Professions Building are located), The Woodlands (where the School of Nursing and The Woodlands Center is located), and Bryan/College Station. The Texas Medical Center, located in Houston, is the largest medical center in the world and is a 75-mile drive from Huntsville. Huntsville is full of Texas history and charm, and this county seat is home to multiple museums, annual festivities, antique stores, year-round outdoor activities, vineyards, golf courses, lakes, and a beautiful state park. In a little over an hour after leaving main campus, you can arrive in downtown Houston. It provides access to large entertainment venues and professional sporting events. If you prefer life on the water, Lake Conroe and Lake Livingston are a short commute, and Galveston Island and the Gulf coast are a two-hour drive. A quick 35-minute drive down I-45 South takes you to The Woodlands, which offers 220 miles of hike and bike trails,150 parks to enjoy, and easy access to numerous shopping, sport, and dining venues. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Transcripts Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research & Goals © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/49097": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Anatomy",
      "description": "Employment @ Sam Houston State University | Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Anatomy Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Application Instructions FAQs Staff Pay Grade Table Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Anatomy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is located at the Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine in Conroe, Texas. Posting Details Come and join the Bearkat community! Named after Texas' legendary hero, General Sam Houston, the university boasts a rich historical legacy that resonates with the spirit of Texas, which provides a balance between a peaceful, natural setting and proximity to urban amenities. With a student population of over 21,000, SHSU offers a vibrant and dynamic community. SHSU has a small town feel with large scale opportunities. Located in the Piney Woods region of East Texas and just an hour drive north of Houston, Huntsville provides area residents with a sense of community and belonging. SHSU offers compelling options for individuals seeking a fulfilling and impactful career including a superior benefit package , competitive salaries and a flexible work environment fostering work/life balance. SHSU offers programs that support a healthy work-life balance, contributing to employee well-being and job satisfaction, as well as, professional development opportunities with our educational assistance and dependent assistance programs. Position Information This position is security-sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215, which authorizes the employer to obtain criminal history record information. Position Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Clinical Anatomy Requisition 202600120F Rank Assistant or Associate Professor FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Full-Time Tenure Track College Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine Department Dept of Clinical Anatomy Open Date 10/29/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/48527 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Lisa Pabst Title Administrative Associate III Clinical Anatomy 925 City Central Ave. Ste. 415 Conroe, Texas 77304 Contact Phone 936-202-5234 Contact Email ldp028@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job The Department of Clinical Anatomy at the Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine at Sam Houston State University is seeking a full-time faculty member experienced in teaching clinical anatomy to medical students or comparable level healthcare professional trainees (e.g. doctorate level physical therapy). Duties of the position will include but are not limited to didactic and lab-based teaching of gross anatomy through full-body cadaver dissection with a particular focus on clinical correlations. The position also involves teaching diagnostic medical imaging, histology, and embryology, with teaching being required in multiple courses. Research activity, service to the college, and student advising and mentoring are also required. Educational Requirements for the Position PhD, MD, DO or equivalent degree in medicine, anatomy, or related field from an accredited university with postdoctoral experience. Experience Required for the Position Candidate should have at least 3 years of experience in an academic institution teaching anatomy to medical students or comparable level healthcare professional trainees. Proficiency at writing board-style (particularly NBOME / NBME ) exam questions will be expected. Other Requirements for the Position The candidate will be required to use curriculum delivery systems such as Blackboard and exam writing software such as Examsoft. Experience using different teaching methods such as case-based learning, ‘flipped classroom’, team-based learning, interactive large group presentation, and audience response systems is preferable. Special Instructions Summary This position is located at the Russell & Glenda Gordy College of Osteopathic Medicine in Conroe, Texas. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sam Houston State University is an “at will” employer. Employees with a contract will have additional terms and conditions. Security-sensitive positions at SHSU require background checks in accordance with Education Code §51.215. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn about this position? The Chronicle of Higher Education TWC - Work in Texas Inside Higher Ed Higher Ed Jobs HERC - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium SHSU Website SHSU Employee Other If your response to the question above was \"SHSU Employee\" please indicate employee's name and department. (Open Ended Question) If your response to the question above was \"Other\" please indicate from what source. (Open Ended Question) Candidate Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae (Faculty) Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Reference Contact Information © Copyright Sam Houston State University. All rights reserved. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
