 Lecturer-Pool FLSA status Exempt Hiring Salary Commensurate with education and experience. Position Category Position Type Part-Time Non-Tenure Track College College of Arts & Media Department Dept of Theatre and Musical Theatre Open Date 06/08/2026 Quicklink https://shsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/47449 Refer Applicants To Contact Name Nicholas Graves Title Department Chair/Professor Sam Houston State University Department of Theatre and Musical Theatre Box 2297 Huntsville, TX 77341 Contact Phone 9362944033 Contact Email nag023@shsu.edu Position Details Duties Performed in the Usual Course of the Job Sam Houston State University ( SHSU ) Department of Theatre & Musical Theatre seeks Lecturer – Pool Faculty to teach musical theatre voice and/or musicianship skills as well as potentially serve as music director and conductor for one or more of the departmental musical productions. Educational Requirements for the Position MM, MFA , MA, or DMA in musical theatre, voice, or related discipline required. Experience Required for the Position Experience teaching musical theatre voice and styles in studio voice classes is required. Musical conducting skills and experience required and accompanist skills preferred. Other Requirements for the Position Special Instructions Summary Please note: References provided in the References section of the application will receive an automated email reference request at the time the application is submitted. Open Until Filled Yes EEO Statement EEO Statement Sam Houston State University is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer and Smoke/Drug-Free Workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, creed, ancestry, marital status, citizenship, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, or protected veteran status. The University takes seriously the initiative to ensure equal opportunity in the workforce and to comply with Title VII as interpreted by the U.S. Supreme Court. Sa